{"abstain":true,"answer":"Page 1 confirms that LangChain can use an existing Qdrant collection, potentially requiring configuration to map Qdrant points into LangChain `Document` objects. If the collection uses named vectors, you can configure which vector name to use.

However, the provided material does not show how to initialize a LangChain Qdrant wrapper for an existing collection without supplying documents or an embedding object. It therefore does not establish a URL-only initialization method.

Page 1 also describes converting incoming text queries into embeddings before nearest-neighbour search. Existing document embeddings address stored data, but that workflow still requires query embedding generation. The material does not specify how to configure this when connecting to your existing collection.","citations":["第1页"]}

